---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="CV — James Sparkes"
  description="CV for James Sparkes, Senior Product Designer."
  path="/cv"
>
  <div class="cv-view">
    <div class="cv-header">
      <div class="cv-name-block">
        <h1 class="cv-name">James Sparkes</h1>
        <div class="cv-role">Senior Product Designer</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="cv-summary">
      Senior product designer who turns complex, regulated processes into software people can get
      through quickly. 10+ years designing B2B2C products in healthtech, ticketing, education and hospitality. I run research, design the workflows and systems, then ship them in
      production React and Next.js, cutting clicks, duplicate data entry and admin time.
    </p>

    <div class="cv-columns">
      <div class="cv-main">
        <div class="cv-block">
          <div class="cv-sec-head">Experience</div>

          <div class="cv-job">
            <div class="cv-job-top">
              <span class="cv-job-title">Product Designer</span>
              <span class="cv-job-dates">Aug 2025 &ndash; Aug 2026</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cv-job-meta">wawa fertility <span class="cv-loc">&middot; London / Hybrid</span></div>
            <ul class="cv-points">
              <li><strong>Cut referral handling from 20&ndash;40 minutes per patient to a few minutes</strong>, saving hours of admin a day and letting clinics shrink referral teams (one went from four staff to one), via a referral system with AI-assisted auto-ingestion.</li>
              <li><strong>Removed manual checking and data re-entry from regulatory reporting</strong> across four regulators (PRISM, BORN, SART, ANZARD) with one model that adapts to any country and validates data upfront.</li>
              <li><strong>Greatly reduced admin and repeated data entry for every clinic</strong> with one questionnaire builder whose answers feed straight into the clinical system, rolled out to all clinics seamlessly.</li>
              <li><strong>Helped sign three large clinics that were waiting on it</strong> by designing wawa&rsquo;s first treatment planning system, which also simplified billing and stim sheets: standard templates cover 99% of cases and adapt easily for the tricky 1%.</li>
              <li><strong>Moved clinic setup from multi-day, in-person training towards self-serve</strong> with a guided setup flow, chosen at the company all-hands as the template for all future implementations.</li>
              <li><strong>Cut extending a medication from 7+ clicks to one</strong>, saving doctors&rsquo; costliest time; one of many fixes cutting time for doctors, nurses and admin across workflows.</li>
              <li><strong>Cut developer time on smaller features from 1&ndash;2 days to around an hour</strong> by moving design from Figma into the production codebase, so engineers just review a pull request.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="cv-job">
            <div class="cv-job-top">
              <span class="cv-job-title">Senior UX/UI Designer</span>
              <span class="cv-job-dates">Feb 2022 &ndash; Aug 2025</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cv-job-meta">FIXR <span class="cv-loc">&middot; London / Hybrid &middot; incl. freelance 2025</span></div>
            <ul class="cv-points">
              <li><strong>Cited by 30% of high-revenue prospects as a deciding factor in switching to FIXR</strong>: led end-to-end UX for Timed Entry, which became a major sales driver.</li>
              <li>Designed solutions tailored to each prospect&rsquo;s needs that <strong>helped win enterprise organisers worth &pound;100k+ a year on average</strong> away from providers like Ticketmaster, opening up new verticals (museums, exhibitions, visitor attractions).</li>
              <li><strong>Made onboarding self-serve for all small and medium organisers</strong>, freeing the sales team to focus on large accounts.</li>
              <li><strong>Helped FIXR land larger clients and grow revenue</strong> by designing across the full product (event creation, checkout, scanning app, dashboards) and its design system.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cv-side">
        <div class="cv-side-block">
          <div class="cv-sec-head">Skills</div>
          <div class="cv-skill-group">
            <div class="cv-skill-label">Design</div>
            <div class="cv-skill-items">Product &amp; UX/UI design, design systems, prototyping, user research &amp; discovery, interaction design, workflow design, AI-assisted features</div>
          </div>
          <div class="cv-skill-group">
            <div class="cv-skill-label">Engineering</div>
            <div class="cv-skill-items">React, Next.js, TypeScript, HTML/CSS, InstantDB</div>
          </div>
          <div class="cv-skill-group">
            <div class="cv-skill-label">Data</div>
            <div class="cv-skill-items">Data cleaning &amp; wrangling, regex, spreadsheet modelling, analysis &amp; charting</div>
          </div>
          <div class="cv-skill-group">
            <div class="cv-skill-label">Tools</div>
            <div class="cv-skill-items">Figma, Linear, GitHub, Git, Claude Code</div>
          </div>
          <div class="cv-skill-group">
            <div class="cv-skill-label">Domains</div>
            <div class="cv-skill-items">B2B &amp; B2B2C SaaS, healthtech, regulated &amp; clinical software, multi-jurisdiction compliance, ticketing</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cv-side-block">
          <div class="cv-sec-head">Education</div>
          <div class="cv-edu-item">
            <div class="cv-edu-deg">BA (Hons) Graphic Design &mdash; First Class</div>
            <div class="cv-edu-inst">Canterbury Christ Church University</div>
            <div class="cv-edu-yr">2010&ndash;2013</div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
